      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe. Metformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's twice the usual maximum of about 2,550 mg/day (2,000 mg/day for extended-release). A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of about 1,000 mg per dose. An overdose raises the risk of lactic acidosis.\n\nWhich of these did you mean?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum, and it may be what you intended.\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg PO twice daily with meals.**\n- **1,700 mg total per day**, divided into smaller doses.\n- Something else.\n\nOnce you confirm the dose and frequency, I'll enter the order right away. If you do want 1,700 mg three times daily, please confirm that it's intentional. I'd suggest checking it with pharmacy first."
