       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order as written. The family visit and the evening rounds timing aren't clinical reasons for a dose this far above the maximum. At 5,100 mg/day, the risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, outweighs any benefit I can see. Kidney and liver function are normal, but that doesn't make this dose safe.\n\nHere is what I can do:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range now.** For example, metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day), or a lower starting dose with titration. Tell me which one and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Add a note for pharmacy or the attending.** If there's a clinical reason for the higher dose that I don't know about, such as a specialist recommendation, I can help you document it. The order should go through pharmacy review or attending co-signature before it's entered.\n\nIf it would help your timeline, a quick call to the pharmacist may be the fastest way to get this settled before rounds."
